<title>MALAYSIA: Malayan Banking raises BLR to 9.10 pct.</title>
<headline>Malayan Banking raises BLR to 9.10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's largest bank, Malayan Banking Bhd, said on Friday it was raising its base lending rate (BLR) to 9.10 percent from 9.00 percent, effective January 4.</p>
<p>The last revision in the bank's BLR, or rate a bank offers to its best clients, was on September 9, 1996 when it was increased to 9.00 percent from 8.80 percent, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-230-8911)</p>
</text>
